<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 October, from 1275 to 1904.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amsterdam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1275">1275 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">751 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Amsterdam is first mentioned in a charter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Count Floris V of Holland granted toll exemption to the people living near the dam on the Amstel. The charter is the earliest document to mention <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a>, then a small fishing settlement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1553">1553 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">473 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Michael Servetus is burned for heresy in Geneva</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>'s council, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-calvin">John Calvin</a>'s backing, had the Spanish physician and theologian Michael Servetus burned for denying the Trinity. His death became a landmark in arguments for religious toleration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1674">1674 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">352 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Dutch army retakes Grave from the French</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege begun on 25 July, the French garrison surrendered the fortress town of Grave, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-brabant">North Brabant</a>, to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> army. The French had held the town since an army under Turenne forced its surrender in 1672.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Franco-Dutch War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1682">1682 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">344 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Penn arrives to found Pennsylvania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-penn">William Penn</a> reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delaware-river">Delaware River</a> aboard the Welcome to take possession of his new colony. He laid out <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> as a planned 'greene Countrie Towne' that later hosted the Declaration of Independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1787">1787 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first Federalist essay is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Writing as 'Publius', <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-hamilton">Alexander Hamilton</a> published the first of 85 essays urging New Yorkers to ratify the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">US Constitution</a>. With Madison and Jay he produced the most influential commentary on the Constitution.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1806">1806 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">220 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon enters Berlin after the Prussian defeat at Jena–Auerstedt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> without a fight, three days after French forces had captured the Prussian capital following their victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a>–Auerstedt. From the city he later issued the Berlin Decree implementing his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-system">Continental System</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jena-auerstedt">Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union forces win the Battle of Brown's Ferry near Chattanooga</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Union forces led by General William Farrar Smith defeated Confederate forces at Brown's Ferry in Hamilton County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, opening a supply line to the besieged city of Chattanooga.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1904">1904 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The New York City Subway opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Interborough Rapid Transit Company opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>'s first underground line, from City Hall to 145th Street. Around 150,000 people rode on the first day of a network that grew into one of the world's largest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li></ol>
